WEBVTT

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.440
As "Prince of the Fateful Eternal Wind,"

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.860
I journey on forever.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.240
I don't get what he's talking about!

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.240
But he's totally sure of himself!

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.580
Thank you so much! Thank you, Sir Hero!

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.080
Please, please, you're too kind.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.710
Now, then...

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.670
I've defeated nearly
all the vicious monsters in this area.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.560
So what's next?

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.680
Our tale takes us to a year ago:

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.240
when the Big Bad--
Koro Sensei--was still a human.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:59.070
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.500
"Nagisa"

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:10.170
"Karma"

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:11.170
"Kaede"

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.500
"Isogai" "Maehara"

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.170
"Rio" "Okuda" "Sugino" "Kanzaki"

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:16.680
"Itona" "Ritsu"

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
"Chiba" "Hayami" "Hinata" "Meg"

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.680
"Hinano" "Takebayashi" "Toka" "Justice"

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:22.680
"Muramatsu" "Kirara" "Yoshida" "Terasaka"

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:24.680
"Okajima" "Hara" "Mimura" "Fuwa" "Sugaya"

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.690
"Karasuma" "Irina"

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.990
"It's Not a Job, It's a Calling"

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.460
"The Temple of Trades"

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.420
"Reception"

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.420
Hey--you've got customers.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.000
No sleeping on the job, losers.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.300
Welcome to the Temple of Trades!

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:57.760
We'll find you a more suitable job
than the one you have now.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.970
Now, what brings you here today?

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:04.930
Truth is, my career development
has reached a dead end.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.060
Oh! And what is your current profession?

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.060
I'm a hero, actually.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.020
Oh, my. You must have worked very hard.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.190
Thank you.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.650
It's all due to my inborn talent
and tireless efforts.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.780
But you're not making much progress.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:25.120
What a waste--seeing that
you've made it as a hero and all.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.370
Ah! I have just the thing!

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.500
Oh? What is it?

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.870
It just so happens a vacancy
opened up the other day:

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.410
The Big Bad in the Castle of Darkness!

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.670
What a fine evil castle this is!

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:43.430
Yes, and if you move in now,
we'll waive the security deposit.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.930
That's helpful.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.100
Why did my predecessor vacate the position?

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.480
It seems he'd run out of room
for growth as the Big Bad.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.690
I see. No career is immune to such concerns.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.190
Oh! There he is!

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.920
Greetings. I am the former Big Bad.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.910
I must thank you for coming all this way.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:10.790
Not at all. In all matters, the handover is key.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.670
From hero to Big Bad...
that's quite a long way to fall.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:18.010
Has human society let you down that badly?

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.340
The element of surprise should go over well.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.510
What a fearsome fellow.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.560
Being the Big Bad is no easy job,
but I think you'll do fine.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.100
Much obliged. I'll give my all to my new life.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.270
And what will you do?

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.940
Yes, well...

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:38.400
There are no longer
any satisfying mysteries for me here.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:43.990
Perhaps I'll head to another world
and start over as a warlock.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.580
Ah, very nice! Please do tell me all about it.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.950
All right, then--do take care.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.000
I will.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.870
"The Big Bad's Chamber"

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:58.130
The Big Bad ensemble! You can have this, too.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.380
How kind. He really has thought of everything.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.340
"The Hero donned the Big Bad's robes"

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.180
Wh-What's the matter?

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.810
Th-This appearance must be
the curse of the Big Bad!

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.020
Suh... suh...

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.770
Ah! Don't look at me--not like this!

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.470
--Splendid!
--Eh?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:22.320
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.590
--Koro-Q.
--Urk! Hey!

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.780
Is this the Big Bad's castle?!

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.990
Hey, Big Bad! Or rather: former hero!

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:32.330
Who are you that you know my true identity?

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.460
Your <i>pupil</i>! Don't tell me you forgot!

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.170
What's the deal with you suddenly
taking off and becoming the Big Bad?!

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:42.340
You see, I couldn't stay motivated
to be a hero anymore.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:46.550
But being the Big Bad is surprisingly boring.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.800
I'm so glad you came to play.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.220
I <i>didn't</i> come to play!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.930
I came to defeat you!

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.810
Well, <i>that's</i> not very nice.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.440
Thanks to you taking over as the new Big Bad,

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.730
monsters are starting to show up again!

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.650
So I'm busy as anything, no time to sleep--

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:05.030
and before I know it, my levels
are through the roof... and I'm a hero!

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:08.490
How marvelous that you've been so successful!

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.120
All thanks to <i>you</i>!

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.330
Oh, dear. Misplaced anger is never good.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.210
And <i>you</i> helped him!

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.500
If you don't like being a hero,
why don't you change jobs, too?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.550
You don't really seem like the hero type.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.670
That stings!

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.430
But...

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.260
Actually, yeah.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.560
I had my suspicions.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:33.720
So it's true.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.600
I mean, if I'm a hero, I'm a hero,
but it's not a great fit.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.230
And I'm worried about room for growth.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.770
That's nice to have.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:42.690
Right?

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.280
Are there any positions that would suit me?

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.900
Well, let's see...

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.740
Ah, here's a good one!

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:49.910
--What is it?
--What is it?

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.870
Here you go: the Reaper!

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.540
Koro-Q!

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:53.870
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.330
"Duo"

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.290
Yes, hello hello hello!

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:55.830
"Comeuppance" "Duo"

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.750
Thank you much!

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.250
Hi! I'm Shiro!

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.790
I'm Yanagisawa.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:04.170
And together, we're One and The Same!

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.460
Great to be here today.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:09.430
We'd be happy if you left here
just remembering our names.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.430
By the way, Shiro...

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:11.970
What is it, Yanagisawa?

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:15.470
That "Shield of Earth" barrier
was really doing you in the other day.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:18.940
Yeah, the government
really will stop at nothing.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:21.940
You almost turned into seared beef tips!

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.190
A short skit:

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.690
"Seared Beef Tips."

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:25.570
Thanks for--

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:26.990
--Koro-Q.
--Koro-Q.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:27.320
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.280
Hello? Mr. Big Bad?

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:34.240
How are things? I'm here for a follow-up visit.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.000
Wow, what a mess!

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:41.460
It's a sin indeed to be too strong...

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.000
You're bored, aren't you.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.920
Yes--terribly.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:48.380
I enjoyed the novelty of it all at first.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:53.510
"Big Bad Banquet"

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:53.760
But no suitable warriors came by to defeat me,

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.680
so I spent day after day tidying the castle,
tending to monsters...

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:01.100
...<i>and</i> placing treasures
in various dungeons near and far!

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.560
You did this yourself?

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.190
One mustn't neglect trap maintenance, either.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:08.400
Brutal--very Big Bad of you.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:12.450
And because of that,
<i>no one</i> ever comes to take me on.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.580
I've got nothing but time on my hands.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.790
That's when I got this idea!

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:18.580
--Yes?
--I'll train up some warriors
to be even mighter than I am!

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.370
--I'll train up some warriors
to be even mighter than I am!

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.840
That's wonderful!

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:25.750
Right?

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.630
--Splendid!
--I know, right?!

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.920
--Splendidly splendid!
--It <i>is</i>, isn't it?

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.380
And so...

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:34.140
...that's what brings me here.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:37.280
I intend to train up warriors
capable of defeating me.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.680
What happened to that pupil of yours?

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.770
He took on the Reaper position
and disappeared somewhere.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.730
Seems it was right up his alley.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.940
That can't be good.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.150
Time for class!

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:56.830
Today I think I'll teach them
how to defeat me with magic potions.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.830
Oh! I've got to return the forbidden tome
I borrowed from Okajima!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.120
See you later!

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.040
Setting aside his past...

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.710
...he <i>is</i> the Big Bad now, right?

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.840
He seems to almost be having fun.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.090
Guess it was right up his alley--

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:12.420
this whole "teacher" gig, that is.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:14.970
You all have room for growth.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.890
Reach the peak too easily,
though, and that will vanish,

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.600
and you'll want to change jobs.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.140
What's he talking about?

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:24.850
You can fail. You can try and try again.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.730
Aim to be fine upstanding warriors.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.400
No, really--<i>what</i> is he <i>talking</i> about?

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:33.150
"Super Cheery"

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.940
Oh! And Okajima--

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.650
Here's that book I borrowed!

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.150
You're giving it back <i>now</i>?!

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.870
Teach is late again today.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.790
I wonder if he's having fun with his students?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.210
Lucky!

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:44.270
"Next Time: Bye-Bye, Big Bad"

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.730
"Ace Sorceress: Confessing the Truth"

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.600
Out with it!

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:51.610
Reveal the ultimate mystery
to satisfy me at last!

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.280
--Yusei Matsui's next project is--
--Hey! Stop that!

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.700
"Jump Editorial Division" "100 Tons"
